From 975e4260a2c847eef9e0c484ec1cc7d41bf0829b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Wojciechowski <robert@wojo.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:53:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1 keeps each stream's latent rows
 on one rank (KV sharding at TP=2)

KV sharding for GLM-5.3-Flash at TP=2 on this stack (f350cd3e + 0001-0109), off by default. Robert's GLM patch 0118
(Python) and the Zig port of Mia's zig-engine recipe, moved to the 1104 engine; the design toward upstream is
ashhart/TensorFold#1431. Design note: docs/glm-port/kv-shard-1104.md.

- What is sharded: each stream's E4M3 latent codes and scales (5,676 B a token over the DSA layers) live on its owner
  rank alone; the pooled index keys (704 B) stay on both ranks, as the indexer runs replicated. A token costs 3,542 B
  a rank instead of 6,380 B, so the same memory holds about 1.8x the tokens.
- The pool's page ids split into two parts, one a rank. A stream takes all its pages from one part; rank 0 places it
  (a kept state's home part first, then the part with fewer live streams, then more free pages). Each stream has a
  second page table for its latent rows; off its owner it points at a trash page. Off, both tables are the same.
- Decode and verify windows: owner-computed attention. The other rank's absorbed queries go to the owner over NCCL,
  the owner attends them, the outputs return. No new kernel.
- Prompts borrow a twin from the other part (both ranks hold the rows until the first verify window gives it back),
  or, with TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_TWINS=0, run owner-computed.
- Kept states: the home rank holds the latent rows; a resume outside its home carries them over in 32 MiB pieces
  (TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_CARRY).
- Refused by name: TP other than 2, a KV cache other than fp8, KV pages off, the MTP drafter, --parallel 1, a part
  under 131,072 tokens.
- --learn-conversations (0109) under sharding: each rank writes the kept state's bytes it holds; rank 0's store
  image stays the unsharded one, its latent rows taken from the home rank, so rows by position stay shared across
  homes and with unsharded states (format word 3 | home << 8 | 2 << 16; unsharded keeps format 1). A read lands in a
  home part rank 0 chooses and then carries, refuses or resumes at home as a state from memory would.
- Telemetry: /health kv_shard and /metrics counters; a layout digest the ranks compare (TF_GLM_KV_SHARD_CHECK).
- GPU check: tf-cuda-test glm-kv-shard-check (both ranks) against an unsharded twin, byte for byte, over seven paths.

Original work by Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
